== Piezoelectric
=== Crystal strcture
Piezoelectric materials (PEM) are materials that can generate an net polarization internally in response to an applied mechanical stress. Without the applied stress, the material is in a neutral state. While the stress applied to the crystal of centro-symmetric materials, the unit cell becomes strained. However, the center of mass of the negative charge still concides with the positive charge so that results in a zero net polarization meaning this crystal strcture is not capable for the PEM. The PEM is always non-centro-symmetric. When stress applied, the center of the mass for the postive and negative charges will displace, result in a net polarization difference showed in @non-centro-crystal. // cite material physics lecture notes. 

#figure(
  image("non-centra-symmetry.png", width: 70%),
  caption: [
    a) The cystal stucture of non-centro-symmetric material. b) The net polarization when stress applied on vertical direction. c) The net polarization when stress applied on horizontal direction.
  ],
)<non-centro-crystal>

=== Piezoelectric effect
The pizeoelectricity can be understood as a linear electromechanical interaction between the mechanical and electrical states. The linearity could be written as @coefficient, 
$ P_i = d_(i j) T_j $<coefficient>
supposed the $T_j$ is the stress along $j$ direction and $P_i$ is the polarization along $i$ direction. The $d_(i j)$ is the piezoelectric coefficient. Air propagates from the top to the bottom, exerting pressure perpendicular to the PEM, which causes charge to be generated in the horizontal direction. 

The piezoelectric effect is reversible, meaning that the material can also deform when an electric field is applied. In this project, the microphone is based on the stress applied on the PEM, and the speaker is based on the electric field applied on the PEM. However, in this project, we focus on the microphone. 
